according to u is js synchronus and the asynchronus in behavior 

js itself is an synchronus behavior and single-threaded but browser and node js provides the enviroment
that helps js to behaves asynchronus through  all process is called "event-loop"


without this process your website can freeze the ui  
button would stop working ,
api would block the page,
apps like whatsaap instagram youtube would broken

Simplest Real-World Analogy

Imagine:

JavaScript = One Chef

The chef can do one thing at a time.

Web APIs = Assistants

Assistants handle:

oven timer
food delivery
phone calls
Event Loop = Manager

Manager checks:

"Chef free?"
If yes → gives next completed task

This is exactly how async JS works.

js can only exicutes callbacks by itself